    "address": "Azartplein, Java-eiland, Amsterdam",
    "bagPand": "NL.IMBAG.Pand.0363100012089568",
    "note": "No installed model, native-kit POI or poi-work-queue task covered this pand (checked by name and landmarkId). No OSM POI exists for it, so a model-local landmarkId is used. It is a genuinely distinctive housing block (curved anthracite front), so the Hotel Jakarta fallback was not needed."
  },
  "architecture": {
    "sources": [
      {
        "url": "https://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woongebouw_Wladiwostok",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-10"
      }
    ],
    "facts": [
      "Designed by Jo Crepain for housing association Het Oosten; built c. 1994 on Java-eiland with 72 rental flats and maisonnettes plus 13 business units.",
      "Nine storeys; the east front on Azartplein is a concave arc of anthracite brick following the tram loop; a stack of planted balconies marks the centre; steps run along the foot of the front.",
      "Pyramide Wonen prize 1998. The name is the Dutch spelling of Vladivostok, a pun on Het Oosten."
    ]
  },
  "measuredBy": {
    "3dbag": "NL.IMBAG.Pand.0363100012089568 LoD2.2: ground 1.5 m NAP, roof 27.6 m above ground, roofMax 29.8 m NAP (mast). The east arc is the ring run from vertex 1 to 57 (about 38 m long); window frames sit on the real 3DBAG wall planes (up to 0.3 m proud of the ring).",
    "front": "twelve window columns (five south of the stack, three in it, four north), eight storey rows above the ground-floor door openings, four balcony levels at 4.8, 10.3, 15.6 and 21.0 m, counted and scaled on the 2018 and 2023 frontal photographs (facade spans 55..1230 px).",
    "rear": "the 2019 rear photograph shows red brick with curved balconies and a stair tower, so the non-front faces are red brick."
  },
